# 120100 is live Mainline; 120105 is Mainline Test (the PTR). Both are listed so
# the addon loads on either without a second TOC -- comma-delimited interface
# versions have been supported since 10.2.7.
## Interface: 120100, 120105
# The same numbers again, as a custom field. GetAddOnMetadata only answers for
# a fixed set of fields plus X- ones, and "Interface" is not among them -- so
# /cshop diag could not report what the addon declares and printed "?" on a
# live client. CI asserts the two lines agree.
## X-Interface: 120100, 120105
## Title: CraftShopper
## Notes: Sends the reagents of the open profession recipe to an Auctionator shopping list.
## Notes-deDE: Schickt die Zutaten des geoeffneten Rezepts auf eine Auctionator-Einkaufsliste.
## Author: Aybee2k8
# A literal version, not the packager's @project-version@ placeholder: that is
# only substituted when a release is built, so a clone or ZIP install would show
# the placeholder itself in the addon list. Bump this with the release tag --
# the release workflow refuses a tag that does not match.
## Version: 0.1.0
## SavedVariables: CraftShopperDB
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Note_06
# The unlocalized fallback goes first: later entries overwrite earlier ones, so
# a locale with no entry of its own still lands in a sensible category.
## Category: Professions
## Category-deDE: Berufe
# Auctionator is listed as an optional dependency purely for load order: the
# client loads OptionalDeps first where they are present, so its API exists by
# the time our first click can happen. The addon degrades to a clear error
# message when it is absent, so it is not a hard dependency.
## OptionalDeps: Auctionator
## AddonCompartmentFunc: CraftShopper_OnAddonCompartmentClick

